     "explanation": "The defining test is usability: a real essential intent is narrow and concrete enough that someone without executive authority could apply it, alone, to a specific Tuesday-afternoon decision. Most mission statements fail precisely because they are written to be broadly agreeable, which makes them too vague to rule anything in or out. Length, legal status, and industry are not what separates the two.",
